# STATUS: draft — needs vendor-baseline + BSP source analysis

## Goal
Port eMMC/SD controller support from Amlogic 5.15 BSP into mainline Linux meson-gx-mmc driver. S905X5M/S7D uses IP derived from G12A/SM1 but with register layout differences (verify against hardware team docs).

## BSP source to diff against
```
DannieDarko/odroid-c5_linux_common_drivers (to be cloned)
├── drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c              (S7D variant logic)
├── arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/s7d_meson_mmc.dtsi
└── arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/s7d_s905x5m_odroidc5.dts (eMMC node)
```

## Mainline file(s) to extend
```
torvalds/linux (v6.16+)
├── drivers/mmc/host/meson-gx-mmc.c
├── arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-s7d.dtsi
└── arch/arm64/boot/dts/amlogic/amlogic-s7d-s905x5m-bm202.dts (reference board — baseline)
```

## Expected diff outline
- compatible string: `"amlogic,s7d-mmc"` (needs DT binding doc in Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mmc/amlogic,meson-gx-mmc.yaml)
- Clock/reset bindings: clock IDs & reset names (SMC1/G12A reference; S7D may differ)
- Register layout: verify eMMC_CFG / eMMC_TIMING vs SM1 — timing register shifts?
- Bus width: emmc 8-bit support (check hw errata vs SM1)
- DTS: eMMC node in amlogic-s7d.dtsi (pinmux/pad groups → s7d pinctrl driver)

## Open questions
- [ ] Does S7D eMMC IP use identical register map as SM1, or new layout?
- [ ] Clock indices: eMMc_clk vs sm1_eMMC_clk — same CLKID enum?
- [ ] Reset indices: eMMC reset line name in Amlogic reset controller?
- [ ] eMMC HS400 tuning: are timing parameters identical, or new calibration?
- [ ] ODroid-C5 PCB: which eMMC socket signal driving — 3.3V only or 1.8V capable?
- [ ] Pinctrl: are eMMC pads in same group as SM1 odroid-c4?

## Upstream submission target
- linux-mmc@vger.kernel.org
- Cc: Ulf Hansson (MMC maintainer), linux-amlogic@lists.infradead.org
- Get_maintainer.pl on patch (TBD)
- Binding doc MUST accompany

## Acceptance criteria
- [ ] BSP driver diffed against mainline (identify deltas)
- [ ] Minimal patch authored (compatible string + binding)
- [ ] Kernel builds clean (CONFIG_MMC_MESON_GX=y)
- [ ] DTS boot w/ eMMC node attached, dmesg shows mmc registration
- [ ] eMMC accessible: `ls /dev/mmcblk*` + basic R/W to partition
- [ ] DT binding YAML doc written & passes yamllint
- [ ] Posted to linux-mmc + Signed-off-by
